Enforce one-active-delivery invariant server-side

A driver may now have at most one request in "claimed" status at a time.

Changes:
- Added `activeRequestId` to `driverRegistry/{driverId}` as the
  authoritative per-driver lock for active deliveries. It is set on
  claim/assignment and cleared on delivery completion, cancellation,
  dispute resolution, and delivery-confirmation timeout.
- `getNextOfferForDriver()` now refuses to issue/reuse an offer while the
  driver has any active claimed delivery.
- `claimWaterRequest()` now rejects claims with `DRIVER_HAS_ACTIVE_DELIVERY`
  inside its Firestore transaction, protected by the registry lock plus a
  defensive fallback query for pre-existing data.
- `dispatcherAssign()` and `dispatcherReassign()` now reject assignments
  that would stack an active delivery on a driver who already has one.
- `isDriverImmediatelyAvailable()` treats a driver with an active delivery
  as not immediately available, so urgent/critical preferred-driver holds
  bypass them correctly.
- Driver portal shows "Complete your current delivery to receive the next
  request" instead of "No deliveries available" when a claimed delivery
  exists.
- Selection logic extracted into `dispatchSelection.ts` and fully unit-tested.
- PRODUCT.md, TECHNICAL.md, and DEVIN.md updated with the new rule and the
  distinction between "online" and "immediately available".

Existing data: registry entries without `activeRequestId` are handled by a
fallback query inside the transaction, so no emergency cleanup is required.
A one-time backfill is recommended to keep the lock consistent.

